exports[`buildPromptDocument — search flow (single inferred method) > renders a single search method with no sensitive params 1`] = `
"<recospec_prompt flow="search-flow" framework="cypress" session="session-1" generated_at="2024-05-06T12:53:20.000Z">
  <role>You are Recospec's recorded test author. The recording below is ground truth: write the test code it describes and do not invent selectors, pages or flows.</role>
  <scenario name="Search Flow" start_url="https://example.com/search" viewport="1280x800" timezone="UTC" captured="2024-05-06" pages="1" steps="2" network_captures="0"/>
  <pages>
    <page class="SearchPage" url="/search">
      <elements>
        <element name="searchInput" tag="input" input_type="search">
          <locator strategy="aria-label">[aria-label=&quot;Search&quot;]</locator>
        </element>
      </elements>
      <methods>
        <method name="search" steps="2">
          <param name="search" type="string"/>
        </method>
      </methods>
    </page>
  </pages>
  <flow>
    <step n="1" page="SearchPage" action="fill" element="searchInput" value="Recospec"/>
    <step n="2" page="SearchPage" action="keypress" key="Enter"/>
  </flow>
  <network_mocks empty="true"/>
  <secrets empty="true"/>
  <fragility_hints empty="true"/>
  <instructions>
    <task>Write the test for the &quot;search-flow&quot; flow recorded above using Cypress (JavaScript): one page object per page plus one scenario that replays the flow.</task>
    <deliverables>
      <file kind="page-object" page="SearchPage" path="cypress/pages/SearchPage.js"/>
      <file kind="scenario" path="cypress/e2e/search-flow.cy.js"/>
    </deliverables>
    <rules>
      <rule>Use only the locators in the pages section. Try each locator first; if it fails, walk its fallback entries in rank order. Never invent selectors.</rule>
      <rule>Treat testid, aria-label, role-name and label locators as durable; css and xpath are last-resort. Check fragility_hints before relying on one.</rule>
      <rule>Expose each method as a page-object method with exactly the listed params and types, and replay the flow steps in order in the scenario.</rule>
      <rule>Implement every assert step in the flow as an assertion on the referenced element.</rule>
      <rule>A section marked empty=&quot;true&quot; means the recording produced no data for it; do not fabricate any.</rule>
      <rule>No sensitive parameters were detected; still never hard-code credentials.</rule>
      <rule>Only mock the requests in network_mocks that an assertion depends on, and strip the Authorization, Cookie, Set-Cookie headers from any fixture.</rule>
      <rule>If the project already has page objects or tests for these pages, extend them with the missing methods instead of duplicating them.</rule>
      <rule>Do not hand-edit recorded locator values to make a test pass; report the failing element so the flow can be re-recorded.</rule>
      <rule>Page objects are plain classes returning Cypress chains; no async/await.</rule>
      <rule>Prefer \`cy.get(&quot;[data-testid=…]&quot;)\`/\`cy.contains\` for the matching strategies; use \`cy.selfHealing\` for elements with fallbacks.</rule>
      <rule>Rely on Cypress retry-ability; never \`cy.wait(&lt;number&gt;)\`.</rule>
    </rules>
    <verification>
      <step>Run npx cypress run and fix failures until the test passes.</step>
      <step>Confirm the generated files contain no literal secret values and no unused locators.</step>
    </verification>
    <output_format>Create the files listed in deliverables, then reply with the files created or modified and the exact command you ran with its result. No other prose.</output_format>
  </instructions>
</recospec_prompt>
"
`;
